# Cast a real spell through the normal key interface until mana sits inside
# the 35-80% band the mana-regen floor fix cares about, then wait several
# turns without resting, with no forced state anywhere. (bd inc-41kg)
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/gates/Options.Dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/orc-mage-seed4-gate.sav \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/mana-regen-cast.keys 4
#
# WHY 35 CASTS OF BURNING HANDS. Henk (the fixture) starts at 72/72 mana.
# Burning Hands (lib/wspells.irh:1061) is Cost 2, Level 1, qval Q_DIR,
# EF_DEFENSIVE only -- no EF_PERSISTANT/EF_LOSEMANA, so it never touches
# held mana (hMana stays 0 the whole script). [RIGHT] answers its direction
# prompt and fires at once, no ENTER. Aimed away from the player rather than
# at '*' (Target Self): Burning Hands centers on EActor when EDir has no X or
# Y component (lib/wspells.irh:1093-1098, the `else` branch of the HIT_SPOT
# dispatch), so '*' would burn the caster himself -- confirmed by reading
# that branch, not guessed. RIGHT crosses open floor (see the arrival dump)
# with nothing standing in it, so every cast fizzles harmlessly and only
# spends mana. Calibrated empirically against the FIXED build, seed 4: 5
# casts -> 69, 10 -> 65, 20 -> 57, 30 -> 48, 35 -> 43, 40 -> 38 (all /72).
# Early casts decline slowly because mana starts near full and the (correct)
# 80%-Concentration floor lets regen partly offset each cast; once mana
# drops under that floor regen stops and the decline is clean. 35 casts
# lands at 43/72 = 59.7%, comfortably inside 35-80% with margin either side.
#
# WHY THE WAIT IS THREE SEARCHES, NOT ONE. KY_CMD_SEARCH (src/Player.cpp)
# grants ACTING for 25 rounds and continues the search on its own, so one
# 's' already spends roughly 25 real turns -- confirmed empirically (turn
# 198001 -> 199561 off a single 's' once mana was near full). Three searches
# buys roughly 75 turns, far more than the "at least one point" the fix's
# own probe check asks for, so an unblocked caster's rise is unmistakable.
#
# WHY THE SAVE AT THE END. Same reason as tools/keys/load-char-sheet.keys:
# it is the read-only channel back to src/Dump.cpp's "Mana: cur/max (spent
# S, held H)" line, which states held explicitly instead of leaving it to be
# inferred from the status line. See tools/keys/save-continue.keys before
# touching the ESC below: it opens the System Menu, not a cancel.

@dump:arrival

d                       # Display Character Sheet -- Concentration is on it
@expect "Gender"
@dump:sheet
ESC                     # leave the sheet, back to play mode

# 35 casts of Burning Hands, aimed RIGHT into open floor.

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

m
@choose "Burning Hands"
RIGHT

